- Best overall next week: Joshua Tree National Park — sunny, mild days (55–60°F), minimal closures, multiple visitor centers open with water/amenities.
- Great alternative: Pinnacles National Park — sunny and a bit warmer (mid‑60s to low‑70s°F near the west entrance), only an occasional crowding alert.
- If you prefer coastal redwoods: Redwood National & State Parks — cool and sunny; note a vehicle closure on the Newton B. Drury Scenic Parkway Dec 1–3 (open to bikes/pedestrians).
- Yosemite is very nice in the Valley this week, but expect major high‑country road closures and weekday trail blasting closures near Vernal/Nevada Falls.
- Consider postponing: Death Valley (widespread road closures from recent flooding), Lassen (main highway closed for winter), parts of Sequoia & Kings Canyon (seasonal road closures).

