- Good but with constraints: Yosemite Valley
  - Evidence: Sunny and mild days in the Valley; however, Tioga Road and Glacier Point Road are closed for winter, and weekday blasting closures affect Mist Trail/JMT to Vernal/Nevada Falls. Best to focus on Valley sights. Source: NPS yose roads/alerts; WeatherAPI Yosemite area.
- Parks to defer this week unless you verify specifics:
  - Death Valley: Many roads closed from 11/18 flooding; while weather is pleasant, check the DEVA conditions page for which canyons/roads/campgrounds are open before committing.
  - Lassen: Park highway (Hwy 89) closed for winter; access is fragmented; some side roads impassible.
  - Sequoia & Kings Canyon: Cedar Grove and Mineral King roads closed for the season; several secondary roads also closed from damage. Foothills and Grant Grove remain accessible, but check chain requirements and daily conditions.

