- URL: https://www.nps.gov/yose/index.htm
- Designation: National Park
- State: CA
- Description: Nearly 1,200 sq mi in the Sierra Nevada, first protected in 1864. Best known for waterfalls, with deep valleys, grand meadows, ancient giant sequoias, vast wilderness, and tranquil High Sierra landscapes.

Location
- Coordinates: 37.84883288, -119.5571873
- Mailing address: PO Box 577, Yosemite National Park, CA 95389

Contacts
- Phone: 209/372-0200
- Email: yose_web_manager@nps.gov

Weather
- Elevation: ~2,000 ft (600 m) to 13,000 ft (4,000 m)
- Precipitation: ~95% falls Oct–May; >75% Nov–Mar
- Snow: Most of the park snow-covered Nov–May; Yosemite Valley can be rainy or snowy during winter storms

Directions
- Year-round access via Highways 41, 140, and 120 (from the west)
- Tioga Pass Entrance (Highway 120 from the east) typically closed approx. Nov–late May/June
- Hetch Hetchy open year-round but may close intermittently due to snow
- Note: GPS directions may be inaccurate
- More info: http://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/driving.htm

Fees (valid 7 consecutive days unless noted)
- Entrance – Private Vehicle: $35 (covers vehicle and all occupants; non-commercial, up to 15 passengers)
- Entrance – Motorcycle: $30 (per motorcycle)
- Entrance – Per Person: $20 (on foot, bicycle, horse, or non-commercial bus/van; 15 and under free)
- Commercial Entrance – Sedan: $25 plus $20 per person, not to exceed $105; commercial use authorization required
- Commercial Entrance – Van: $125; authorization required
- Commercial Entrance – Mini-bus: $200; authorization required
- Commercial Entrance – Motor Coach: $300; authorization required
- Entrance – Non-commercial Groups: $20 per person, up to $300 per vehicle; 15 and under free
- Entrance – Education/Academic Groups: $0 with approved educational fee waiver (for accredited or tax-exempt educational/scientific groups on related, non-primarily recreational trips)
- Commercial Entrance – Per Person: $20 (note: also states $25 plus $20 per person, not to exceed $105; authorization required)

Passes
- Annual Entrance – Park: $70 (free entrance to Yosemite for 12 months from purchase)

Operating Hours
- Yosemite National Park: Open 24 hours/day, 365 days/year
- Hetch Hetchy: Open sunrise to sunset daily for day visitors; road closed to all vehicles from sunset to sunrise; overnight access only for permitted backpackers (road still closed to vehicles at night)

