Tool `National Parks:getParkDetails` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'deva'} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 2659 tokens): - Name: Death Valley National Park (code: deva)
- Designation: National Park; States: CA, NV
- URL: https://www.nps.gov/deva/index.htm
- Description: Below-sea-level basin known for drought and record summer heat, contrasted by winter snow on peaks, rare wildflower blooms after rains, and lush oases supporting diverse life.

Weather
- Spring: Most popular; warm/sunny; possible wildflowers.
- Summer: Starts early; by May, scorching heat.
- Autumn: Late October arrival; warm, pleasant, clear.
- Winter: Cool days, chilly nights; rare rain; snow-capped peaks and low-angled light offer excellent exploring conditions.

Directions
- Info: Multiple entrances; see best travel routes.
- Directions URL: http://www.nps.gov/deva/planyourvisit/directions.htm

