Tool `National Parks:getParkDetails` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'seki'} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 2778 tokens): - Name: Sequoia & Kings Canyon National Parks (code: seki)
- Designation: National Parks; State: CA
- Website: https://www.nps.gov/seki/index.htm
- Overview: Huge mountains, rugged foothills, deep canyons, vast caverns, and the world’s largest trees (giant sequoias). Learn about plants, animals, and conservation threats; even ancient sequoias are vulnerable.
- Weather (varies greatly with elevation):
  - Summer: Sequoia groves comfortable; foothills hot/dry; snow lingers on high passes.
  - Fall: Ranges from summer-like to winter-like.
  - Winter: Snow in sequoia groves, rain in foothills; be prepared for tire chains.
  - Spring: Great for foothill hikes; snowmelt begins at higher elevations.
- Directions:
  - Hwy 180 from Fresno → Kings Canyon NP; continues ~30 miles east to Cedar Grove.
  - Hwy 198 from Visalia via Three Rivers → Sequoia NP; inside the parks becomes Generals Highway, connecting 198 to 180.
  - Vehicles over 22 ft should enter via Hwy 180.
  - Winter: Generals Highway between parks often closes; chains may be required; no east–west roads cross the parks.
  - Directions info: http://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/directions.htm
