Tool `National Parks:getParkDetails` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'pinn'} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 2885 tokens): Pinnacles National Park (code: pinn)
- URL: https://www.nps.gov/pinn/index.htm
- Designation: National Park
- State: CA

Overview
- Formed by volcanic eruptions ~23 million years ago; landscape of rocky spires and deep canyons.
- Habitats include chaparral, oak woodlands, and cool shaded canyon floors.

Location
- Coordinates: 36.49029208, -121.1813607
- Address: 5000 East Entrance Road, Paicines, CA 95043

Weather
- Mediterranean climate. Hot, dry summers often above 100°F; winters mild with highs in the 60s.
- Inland location yields wider seasonal variation and large day–night temperature swings year-round.

Getting There
- West Entrance: via Hwy 101 through Soledad to Hwy 146.
- East Entrance: via Hwy 25 through Hollister (from the north) or via King City then Bitter Water Rd (G‑13) (from the south).
- Note: No through road between east and west entrances.
- Directions: http://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/directions.htm

Operating Hours
- East Side Entrance: open 24/7, including holidays.
- West Side Entrance: open daily 7:30 AM–8:00 PM; access to Prewett Point, Balconies, and Juniper Canyon trails. One-lane, narrow, winding road; oversize vehicles should use the east side.

