  - Aberdeen saw significant weekend nighttime increases: ambulance call-outs +17.4% (effect size 7.061; 95% CI 3.902–10.220; p<0.001) and reported crimes +7.9% (3.187; 0.564–5.810; p=0.017; not robust across sensitivity analyses).
  - Glasgow results were not significant/robust.
  - Suggests impact depends on number/capacity/type of premises; informs licensing policy design.

