Tool `Paper Search:search_arxiv` with Parameter {'query': 'NYUTron electronic health records readmission Nature Medicine 2023', 'max_results': 10} on Paper Search succeeded. Result (summarized from 5116 tokens): - AnyTalker: Scaling Multi-Person Talking Video Generation with Interactivity Refinement (arXiv:2511.23475v1, cs.CV)
  - Authors: Zhizhou Zhong et al.
  - Proposes AnyTalker, a multi-person, extensible multi-stream framework for audio-driven talking video generation.
  - Key method: identity-aware attention in a Diffusion Transformer that iteratively processes identity–audio pairs, enabling arbitrary scaling to many identities.
  - Training uses only single-person videos to learn multi-person patterns; interactivity refined with few real multi-person clips.
  - Contributes a targeted metric and dataset to evaluate naturalness and interactivity.
  - Results: strong lip-sync, visual quality, and natural interactivity with favorable data cost vs. scalability.

- Convergence and front position for an FKPP-type free boundary problem (arXiv:2511.23457v1, math.AP; math.PR)
  - Authors: Julien Berestycki; Sarah Penington; Oliver Tough
  - Proves convergence of a free boundary problem (hydrodynamic limit of N-BBM) to the minimal traveling wave for initial data with sufficiently fast decay.
  - Derives necessary and sufficient conditions for Bramson-type front asymptotics: L_t = √2 t − (3/(2√2)) log t + c + o(1).
  - Extends to a β-parameterized problem, revealing pulled, pushed, and “pushmi-pullyu” regimes; provides sharp convergence conditions and precise front-position asymptotics—first such results in pushed/pushmi-pullyu regimes.

- From metallicity distributions to mutual information: A new perspective on stellar halo assembly (arXiv:2511.23452v1, astro-ph.GA; astro-ph.CO)
  - Authors: Amit Mondal; Biswajit Pandey
  - Introduces mutual information (MI) between angular position and metallicity to quantify spatial–chemical coupling in Aquarius Milky Way–mass halos.
  - Finds diverse MDFs reflecting stochastic assembly; low-metallicity stars show higher anisotropy and clustering; removing bound satellites reduces anisotropy.
  - MI grows with radius and saturates; residual inner-halo coupling indicates incomplete phase mixing.
  - Positions information-theoretic diagnostics as a bridge to compare simulations with upcoming survey data.

- COMPAS: A Distributed Multi-Party SWAP Test for Parallel Quantum Algorithms (arXiv:2511.23434v1, quant-ph)
  - Authors: Brayden Goldstein-Gelb et al.
  - Architecture for multivariate trace estimation across interconnected QPUs using pre-shared Bell pairs.
  - Achieves constant depth overhead and Bell-pair consumption linear in circuit width; simultaneously optimal in depth and GHZ width.
  - Includes analysis of network-level errors and simulations under circuit-level noise; suitable for near-term modular hardware.

- Consensus Tree Estimation with False Discovery Rate Control via Partially Ordered Sets (arXiv:2511.23433v1, stat.ME)
  - Authors: Maria Alejandra Valdez Cabrera; Amy D Willis; Armeen Taeb
  - Recasts consensus tree estimation as structured feature selection over a partial order on leaf-labeled trees.
  - Defines true/false discoveries and provides an estimator with finite-sample, model-free FDR control; assesses feature stability.
  - Handles unequal leaf sets and non-binary trees by collapsing weakly supported structure.
  - Applications include deep branching uncertainty and archaeal origin of eukaryotes; integrates multiple testing with tree estimation.

- A measurement of H0 from DESI DR1 using energy densities (arXiv:2511.23432v1, astro-ph.CO)
  - Authors: Alex Krolewski et al.
  - Low-redshift, standard-ruler–independent H0 via calibrating total energy density: anchor photon density; use BBN baryon-to-photon and clustering-based baryon-to-matter ratios to get present-day matter density; combine with Ωm from BAO ratios to infer critical density and H0.
  - Validated on N-body mocks and theory vectors for ΛCDM/EDE.
  - Result: H0 = 69.0 ± 2.5 km s⁻¹ Mpc⁻¹; examines sensitivity to non-standard dark energy. Future DESI/Euclid to refine tests of Hubble tension.

