- 2511.23473v1 — ThetaEvolve: Test-time Learning on Open Problems (cs.LG; cs.CL; 2025-11-28)
  - Authors: Yiping Wang et al.
  - Open-source framework that scales in-context learning and RL at test time to evolve programs for open optimization problems, simplifying and extending AlphaEvolve.
  - Features: Single LLM, large program database, batch sampling, lazy penalties, optional reward shaping. Enables models to learn evolving strategies (not just inference-only).
  - Results: Small open-source model (DeepSeek-R1-0528-Qwen3-8B) achieves new best-known bounds on circle packing and first auto-correlation inequality; RL-at-test-time consistently outperforms inference-only baselines; RL checkpoints transfer and progress faster on trained and unseen tasks.
