- 2511.23469v1 — Visual Generation Tuning (cs.CV; 2025-11-28)
  - Authors: Jiahao Guo et al.
  - VGT enables visual generation in pretrained VLMs via efficient tuning, mitigating alignment costs and accelerating continuous-space autoregressive modeling (~20× speedup).
  - Method: Discards pixel-level VAEs; introduces VGT-AE aligning VLM semantic encoders with latent representations of pixel decoders.
  - Results: Image reconstruction 26.67 PSNR, 0.50 rFID at 28× compression (beats specialized VAEs); generation SOTA among autoregressive models: 0.77 GenEval, 78.73 DPG-Bench; strong scaling and generality across VLMs.
  - Code: https://github.com/hustvl/VGT
  - Links: arXiv http://arxiv.org/abs/2511.23469v1 | PDF https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.23469v1

- 2511.23463v1 — Kinetic Mixing and the Phantom Illusion: Axion-Dilaton Quintessence in Light of DESI DR2 (astro-ph.CO; hep-ph; 2025-11-28)
  - Authors: Michael W. Toomey et al.
  - Studies kinetically mixed axion–dilaton (KMIX) quintessence that can appear phantom in CPL analyses without true phantom behavior.
  - Pipeline: Normalizing flows learn a theory-informed prior on (w0, wa) from KMIX realizations and map CPL parameters back to KMIX; importance-sampling pre-computed CPL chains yields direct constraints on KMIX efficiently.
  - Results: Planck+DESI DR2 BAO: KMIX supported at 2.5σ vs base CPL fit at 3.1σ; with SNe, preference >3σ for Union3 
