Tool `Paper Search:search_arxiv` with Parameter {'query': 'RETFound retinal foundation model 2023 nature', 'max_results': 10} on Paper Search succeeded. Result (summarized from 4699 tokens): Here are concise summaries of the included papers, highlighting problems, methods, key findings, and resources:

- Video-R2: Reinforcing Consistent and Grounded Reasoning in Multimodal Language Models (cs.CV)
  Authors: Muhammad Maaz; Hanoona Rasheed; Fahad Shahbaz Khan; Salman Khan
  Problem: Video reasoning often looks convincing but is logically inconsistent or weakly grounded in visual evidence.
  Contributions:
  - Define two diagnostics: Think Answer Consistency (TAC) and Video Attention Score (VAS) to quantify alignment between reasoning/answers and reliance on visual vs textual cues.
  - Show MLLMs rely heavily on linguistic priors across 11 video reasoning benchmarks.
  - Propose a reinforcement-learning post-training pipeline combining timestamp-aware SFT with Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO) guided by a Temporal Alignment Reward (TAR) to improve temporal precision and reasoning consistency.
  Results: Higher TAC, VAS, and accuracy across multiple benchmarks; improved temporal alignment and causal coherence lead to more accurate, trustworthy video understanding.
  Resources: Code, dataset, and model to be open-sourced.

- Video-CoM: Interactive Video Reasoning via Chain of Manipulations (cs.CV)
  Authors: Hanoona Rasheed; Mohammed Zumri; Muhammad Maaz; Ming-Hsuan Yang; Fahad Shahbaz Khan; Salman Khan
  Problem: Most MLLMs “think about videos” in text after a single encoding, causing a semantic bottleneck and shallow visual reasoning.
  Contributions:
  - New paradigm: Interactive Video Reasoning—models “think with videos” by iteratively manipulating visual inputs.
  - Model: Video-CoM reasons via a Chain of Manipulations (CoM) to gather/refine evidence.
  - Dataset: Video-CoM Instruct (18K) for multi-step manipulation reasoning.
  - Training: SFT plus RL via GRPO with step-level reasoning rewards (beyond sparse answer rewards) to promote grounded, consistent reasoning.
  Results: Strong performance on 9 benchmarks, +3.6% over recent SOTA while training on only 25K SFT and 3K GRPO video samples; ablations show improved accuracy and interpretability with reasoning-aware rewards.
  Code: https://github.com/mbzuai-oryx/Video-CoM

- Thinking by Doing: Building Efficient World Model Reasoning in LLMs via Multi-turn Interaction (cs.AI)
  Authors: Bao Shu; Yan Cai; Jianjian Sun; Chunrui Han; En Yu; Liang Zhao; Jingcheng Hu; Yinmin Zhang; Haoran Lv; Yuang Peng; Zheng Ge; Xiangyu Zhang; Daxin Jiang; Xiangyu Yue
  Problem: Rigid reasoning pipelines hinder efficient world-model reasoning in interactive environments.
  Contributions (WMAct):
  - Reward rescaling based on action efficacy to reduce redundancy and encourage purposeful interaction.
  - Interaction frequency annealing to progressively limit allowed turns, compelling internalization of dynamics.
  Results: Solves Sokoban, Maze, Taxi tasks in a single turn where multiple were previously needed; strong transferability and improved performance on reasoning benchmarks.

- AnyTalker: Scaling Multi-Person Talking Video Generation with Interactivity Refinement (cs.CV)
  Authors: Zhizhou Zhong; Yicheng Ji; Zhe Kong; Yiying Liu; Jiarui Wang; Jiasun Feng; Lupeng Liu; Xiangyi Wang; Yanjia Li; Yuqing She; Ying Qin; Huan Li; Shuiyang Mao; Wei Liu; Wenhan Luo
  Problem: Audio-driven multi-person talking video generation is limited by data scarcity and difficulty ensuring coherent interactivity.
  Contributions:
  - Extensible multi-stream Diffusion Transformer with identity-aware attention that iteratively processes identity–audio pairs, enabling arbitrary scaling of drivable identities.
  - Training pipeline uses only single-person videos to learn multi-person speaking patterns, then refines interactivity with a small number of real multi-person clips.
  - Introduce a metric and dataset to evaluate naturalness and interactivity.
  Results: Strong lip-sync, visual quality, and natural interactivity; favorable balance between data cost and identity scalability.

