Tool `Paper Search:search_arxiv` with Parameter {'query': 'A foundation model for generalizable disease detection in retinal images 2023', 'max_results': 10} on Paper Search succeeded. Result (summarized from 4699 tokens): - Video-R2: Reinforcing Consistent and Grounded Reasoning in Multimodal Language Models
  - Problem: Video reasoning traces in MLLMs can be persuasive yet logically inconsistent or weakly grounded in visuals; models over-rely on linguistic priors.
  - Diagnostics: Introduces Think Answer Consistency (TAC) for reasoning–answer alignment and Video Attention Score (VAS) for reliance on visual vs textual cues. Analysis across 11 video reasoning benchmarks shows heavy linguistic prior dependence.
  - Method: Two-stage post-training—timestamp-aware supervised fine-tuning plus Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO) with a new Temporal Alignment Reward (TAR) to encourage temporally aligned, causally coherent reasoning.
  - Results: Consistently higher TAC, VAS, and accuracy across multiple benchmarks, yielding more accurate and trustworthy video understanding. Code, dataset, and model to be open-sourced.

- Video-CoM: Interactive Video Reasoning via Chain of Manipulations
  - Paradigm: Moves from “thinking about videos” to “thinking with videos” by turning video into an active workspace. The model performs iterative visual actions (Chain of Manipulations) to gather/refine evidence.
  - Data and Training: Video-CoM Instruct (18K) for multi-step manipulation reasoning; supervised learning (25K videos) plus GRPO with reasoning-aware, step-level rewards (3K videos).
  - Outcomes: Strong results on nine video reasoning benchmarks, +3.6% average over recent SOTA with far fewer training samples; improved accuracy and interpretability. Code: https://github.com/mbzuai-oryx/Video-CoM

- Thinking by Doing (WMAct): Efficient World Model Reasoning via Multi-turn Interaction
  - Goal: Build robust, efficient world-model reasoning without rigid, structured reasoning.
  - Mechanisms: Reward rescaling based on action efficacy to reduce redundancy; interaction frequency annealing to progressively limit allowed turns, pushing internalization of dynamics.
  - Results: On Sokoban, Maze, Taxi, WMAct enables single-turn solutions for tasks that previously needed multiple interactions and improves transferability across reasoning benchmarks.

- AnyTalker: Scaling Multi-Person Talking Video Generation with Interactivity Refinement
  - Architecture: Extensible multi-stream Diffusion Transformer with identity-aware attention that iteratively processes identity–audio pairs, enabling arbitrary scaling of drivable identities.
  - Training: Learns multi-person speaking patterns using only single-person videos; interactivity refined with a small number of real multi-person clips.
  - Evaluation: Introduces a targeted metric and dataset for naturalness and interactivity. Achieves strong lip sync, visual quality, and natural interactivity while balancing data costs and scalability.

- ThetaEvolve: Test-time Learning on Open Problems
  - Contribution: Open-source framework that streamlines and extends AlphaEvolve with a single LLM, enabling efficient in-context learning and reinforcement learning at test time.
  - Components: Large program database for exploration, batch sampling, lazy penalties to discourage stagnation, and optional reward shaping for stable signals.
  - Achievements: A small open-source model (DeepSeek-R1-0528-Qwen3-8B) attains new best-known bounds on circle packing and the first auto-correlation inequality. RL at test time consistently outperforms inference-only; RL-trained checkpoints show faster progress and better final performance on trained and unseen tasks. Code: https://github.com/ypwang61/ThetaEvolve

