Tool `Paper Search:search_arxiv` with Parameter {'query': 'Articulate Medical Intelligence Explorer AMIE clinical conversations 2024', 'max_results': 10} on Paper Search succeeded. Result (summarized from 10023 tokens): Here’s a concise roundup of the papers with key problems, methods, and results.

- 2511.23476v1 — Thinking by Doing: Building Efficient World Model Reasoning in LLMs via Multi-turn Interaction (cs.AI; 2025-11-28)
  - Proposes WMAct to internalize world models via efficient interaction and active reasoning without rigid structured reasoning.
  - Two mechanisms: (1) reward rescaling based on action efficacy to reduce redundancy and incentivize purposeful interaction; (2) interaction frequency annealing to progressively cap turns, pushing internalization over reliance on feedback.
  - Results: On Sokoban, Maze, Taxi, resolves tasks in single turn that previously needed multiple; strong transfer to complex environments and improved reasoning benchmarks.

- 2511.23475v1 — AnyTalker: Scaling Multi-Person Talking Video Generation with Interactivity Refinement (cs.CV; 2025-11-28)
  - Multi-person audio-driven talking video generation with an extensible multi-stream architecture.
  - Introduces identity-aware attention in a Diffusion Transformer to iteratively process identity–audio pairs, enabling arbitrary identity scaling.
  - Training uses only single-person videos to learn multi-person patterns, then refines interactivity with few real multi-person clips.
  - Adds a metric and dataset to evaluate naturalness and interactivity. Achieves strong lip sync, visual quality, and natural interactivity with good data cost/identity scalability trade-off.

- 2511.23473v1 — ThetaEvolve: Test-time Learning on Open Problems (cs.LG; cs.CL; 2025-11-28)
  - Open-source framework that extends AlphaEvolve with a single LLM and test-time reinforcement learning to continually learn strategies for open optimization problems.
  - Features: large program database, batch sampling, lazy penalties to avoid stagnation, optional reward shaping; efficiently scales in-context + RL at test time.
  - Achieves new best-known bounds on circle packing and the first auto-correlation inequality with a small open-source model (DeepSeek-R1-0528-Qwen3-8B).
  - RL at test time outperforms inference-only across two models and four tasks; trained checkpoints show faster progress and better final performance, including on unseen tasks.
  - Code: https://github.com/ypwang61/ThetaEvolve

- 2511.23469v1 — Visual Generation Tuning (cs.CV; 2025-11-28)
  - VGT unlocks visual generation in pretrained VLMs via efficient tuning, avoiding pixel-level VAEs used by diffusion transformers.
  - VGT-AE aligns VLM semantic encoders with latent pixel decoders; accelerates continuous-space autoregressive modeling (~20× speedup).
  - Image reconstruction: 26.67 PSNR, 0.50 rFID at 28× compression, outperforming specialized VAEs.
