  - 64% were asymptomatic; none met IDSA criteria for testing.
  - Symptomatic patients more often had positive UA (72.2% vs 43.8%; p=0.06) and were more often prescribed antibiotics for positive UA (61.5% vs 14.3%; p=0.0128) and even negative UA (20.0% vs 0%; p=0.05).
  - Significant discordance highlights need for educational interventions to reduce unnecessary UA and antibiotic use.

