  - Objective: Evaluate AI for translating complex spine MRI report terminology into lay language to improv
Tool `Paper Search:search_pubmed` with Parameter {'query': 'electronic health record transformer readmission 2024 2025', 'max_results': 15} on Paper Search succeeded. Result: [{"paper_id":"41126229","title":"Explainable AI for infection prevention and control: modeling CPE acquisition and patient outcomes in an Irish hospital with transformers.","authors":"Pham MK; Mai TT; Crane M; Brennan R; Ward ME; Geary U; Byrne D; O'Connell B; Bergin C; Creagh D; McDonald N; Bezbradica M","abstract":"Carbapenemase-Producing Enterobacteriace (CPE) poses a critical concern for infection prevention and control in hospitals. However, predictive modeling of previously highlighted CPE-associated risks such as readmission, mortality, and extended length of stay (LOS) remains underexplored, particularly with modern deep learning approaches. This study introduces an eXplainable AI (XAI) modeling framework to investigate CPE impact on patient outcomes from Electronic Medical Records (EMR) data of an Irish hospital.","doi":"10.1186/s12911-025-03214-1","published_date":"2025-01-01T00:00:00","pdf_url":"","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41126229/","source":"pubmed","updated_date":"2025-01-01T00:00:00","categories":"","keywords":"","citations":0,"references":"","extra":""}]
Tool `Paper Search:search_pubmed` with Parameter {'query': 'ophthalmology foundation model fundus OCT foundation model 2023 2024', 'max_results': 15} on Paper Search succeeded. Result (summarized from 2350 tokens): Here is a concise synthesis of the provided articles, preserving key aims, methods, findings, and implications:

1) Paper ID: 41258201
- Title: The role of full-field stimulus threshold in evaluating Bietti crystalline dystrophy
- Authors: Wang J; Luo J; Yin S; Zhang H; Zhao H; Feng Z; Dimopoulos IS; Zhang J; Guan N; Chen J; Li H; Bhari M; Liang C; Zhu J; Wei W
- Year/DOI: 2025; 10.1007/s00417-025-07029-8
- Aim/Design: To determine whether full-field stimulus threshold (FST) is an effective visual function method for Bietti crystalline dystrophy (BCD) and whether it can replace traditional tests, especially in low-vision cases.
- Key point: Study designed to evaluate FST’s utility in BCD; abstract does not report outcomes.

2) Paper ID: 41042360
- Title: Development and validation of machine learning for pathological changes in high myopia patients with tessellated fundus: a cross-sectional study
- Authors: Zuo H; Huang H; Huang B; He J; Liu X; Huang L; Bi F; Huang M
- Year/DOI: 2025; 10.1007/s00417-025-06988-2
- Problem: Early pathological changes in high myopia with tessellated fundus are hard to detect with OCT and fundus imaging.
- Approach: Cross-sectional development/validation of machine learning models using lifestyle and clinical parameters to identify at-risk patients.
- Key point: Proposes ML-based early detection strategy; performance metrics not provided in abstract.

3) Paper ID: 39467145
- Title: Retinal G-protein-coupled receptor deletion exacerbates AMD-like changes via the PINK1-parkin pathway under oxidative stress
- Authors: Guo Y; Chen S; Guan W; Xu N; Zhu L; Du W; Liu Z; Fong HKW; Huang L; Zhao M
- Year/DOI: 2024; 10.1096/fj.202401160RR
- Context: High-fat diet (HFD) increases oxidative stress, disrupting RPE via lipid dysregulation/inflammation; retinal G-protein-coupled receptor deletion (RGR-d) identified in drusen.
- Design: In vivo and in vitro assessment of how RGR-d exacerbates AMD-like changes under oxidative stress.
- Findings:
  - At 12 months, RGR-d + HFD mice showed fundus atrophy; angiography: narrower retinal vessels and reduced peripheral perfusion.
  - ERG: a-/b-wave amplitudes trended lower at 12 months but not statistically significant.
  - Morphology: thinner, more fragile retina; disordered/discontinuous pigment; TEM showed thickened Bruch’s membrane at choriocapillaris, disorganized outer nuclear layer with reduced nuclear density.
  - KEGG analysis: significantly lower 25(OH)-vitamin D3 metabolites in RGR-d + HFD.
  - Mechanism: Under oxidative stress, RGR-d localized to mitochondria and reduced PINK1-parkin pathway activity, disrupting mitophagy.
- Conclusions: RGR-d mice on HFD serve as a new dry AMD model; HFD-induced oxidative stress with mitochondrial RGR-d accumulation impairs mitophagy and exacerbates AMD-like damage.

4) Paper ID: 39139546
- Title: Artificial Intelligence to Facilitate Clinical Trial Recruitment in Age-Related Macular Degeneration
- Authors: Williamson DJ; Struyven RR; Antaki F; Chia MA; Wagner SK; Jhingan M; Wu Z; Guymer R; Skene SS; Tammuz N; Thomson B; Chopra R; Keane PA
- Year/DOI: 2024; 10.1016/j.xops.2024.100566
- Aim: Explore how AI can improve recruitment of patients with geographic atrophy (GA) for AMD clinical trials amid many concurrent studies.
- Key point: Positions AI as a tool to streamline/transform trial recruitment; abstract does not detail specific models or results.

