Tool `Paper Search:search_arxiv` with Parameter {'query': 'electronic health records transformer 2023 2024 2025', 'max_results': 15} on Paper Search succeeded. Result (summarized from 6339 tokens): - Video-R2: Reinforcing Consistent and Grounded Reasoning in Multimodal LLMs (arXiv:2511.23478)
  - Problem: Video “thinking” traces can be logically inconsistent and weakly grounded in visuals.
  - Diagnostics: Think Answer Consistency (TAC) aligns reasoning with answers; Video Attention Score (VAS) quantifies reliance on visual vs textual cues.
  - Method: Timestamp-aware SFT + GRPO with a Temporal Alignment Reward (TAR) to improve temporal precision and causal coherence.
  - Results: Higher TAC, VAS, and accuracy across 11 video reasoning benchmarks. Code, data, model to be open-sourced.

- Video-CoM: Interactive Video Reasoning via Chain of Manipulations (arXiv:2511.23477)
  - Paradigm: “Think with videos” by iteratively manipulating visual input (Chain of Manipulations) to gather/verify evidence.
  - Data/Training: Video-CoM Instruct (18K) for multi-step manipulation; RL via reasoning-aware GRPO with step-level rewards.
  - Performance: +3.6% average over recent SOTA across 9 benchmarks using only 25K SFT and 3K RL samples; improved accuracy and interpretability.
  - Code: https://github.com/mbzuai-oryx/Video-CoM

- Thinking by Doing (WMAct): Efficient World Model Reasoning via Multi-turn Interaction (arXiv:2511.23476)
  - Goal: Internalize world models without rigid structured reasoning; leverage active interaction.
  - Key mechanisms: (1) Reward rescaling by action efficacy to reduce redundancy; (2) Interaction frequency annealing to force condensed learning.
  - Results: Solves Sokoban, Maze, Taxi in fewer (often single) turns; strong transfer to complex environments; improved reasoning benchmarks.

- AnyTalker: Scaling Multi-Person Talking Video Generation (arXiv:2511.23475)
  - Architecture: Extensible multi-stream Diffusion Transformer with identity-aware attention over iterated identity–audio pairs; scales to arbitrary identities.
  - Training: Primarily single-person videos; refine interactivity with few real multi-person clips.
  - Contributions: New metric and dataset for multi-person interactivity; strong lip-sync, visual quality, natural interactivity with favorable data/identity scalability trade-off.

- Lyapunov-Based Small-Gain Theorem for Fixed-Time Stability (arXiv:2511.23474)
  - Result: Small-gain theorem for interconnections where subsystems admit fixed-time ISS Lyapunov functions (FxT-ISS); a nonlinear small-gain condition ensures overall FxTS.
  - Significance: Extends Lyapunov small-gain theory to fixed-time stability; examples include fixed-time feedback optimization without time-scale separation.

- ThetaEvolve: Test-time Learning on Open Problems (arXiv:2511.23473)
  - Framework: Open-source, single-LLM extension of AlphaEvolve enabling in-context and RL at test-time; large program DB, batch sampling, lazy penalties, optional reward shaping.
  - Achievements: Small open-source model (DeepSeek-R1-0528-Qwen3-8B) attains new best-known bounds (circle packing; first auto-correlation inequality).
  - Findings: RL at test-time consistently outperforms inference-only; learned evolving strategies transfer to unseen tasks.
  - Code: https://github.com/ypwang61/ThetaEvolve

- RapunSL: Quantum Separation Logic with Linear Combination and Mixing (arXiv:2511.23472)
  - Concepts: Basis-locality (reduce superposition reasoning to pure states) and outcome-locality (reduce mixed states from measurement to pure states).
  - Logic: Adds linear combination and mixing connectives to separation/disentanglement for scalable quantum program verification.
  - Evidence: Challenging case studies show dramatic scalability gains.

- HOTIs: Wilson Loops, Symmetries, and Selective Bulk-Boundary Correspondence (arXiv:2511.23471)
  - Models: Chiral-symmetric Bloch Hamiltonians generalizing π-flux square lattice; separable vs nonseparable with extended/diagonal hopping.
  - Invariants: Product of subsystem chiral winding numbers works for separable but fails for nonseparable.
  - New tools: Gauge-independent mirror-filtered windi
