- Scope: Chiral-symmetric Bloch Hamiltonians generalizing the π-flux square lattice (quadrupole insulator), covering separable and nonseparable models with extended/diagonal hopping.
- Separable case: Product of subsystem chiral winding numbers predicts zero-energy corner states.
- Nonseparable case: Above invariant fails; develop momentum-space diagnostics.
- New invariants: Gauge-independent mirror-filtered winding numbers for Wannier Hamiltonians (mirror-projected occupied subspace). Adapt periodicized Wilson lines from chiral Floquet theory to momentum-dependent chiral operators, defining invariants tied to Wannier gaps.
- Phenomena: Specific mirror-symmetry breaking yields selective boundary gap closings (one boundary orientation), with bulk and other boundaries gapped; extends to 3D hinge- and corner-selective transitions.
- Impact: Clarifies roles of chiral/mirror symmetries and Wilson loops; highlights open challenges for general nonseparable models.

