  - Problem: Offline RL on suboptimal/fragmented data hampers reward propagation; generative stitching often stays within behavior support or violates dynamics.
  - Method: ASTRO augments data with novel, dynamics-consistent stitched trajectories:
    - Learns temporal-distance representations to pick distinct, reachable stitch targets.
    - Dynamics-guided stitch planner produces connecting actions using Rollout Deviation Feedback (gap between target and executed state sequences) to improve feasibility/reachability.
  - Results: Outperforms prior augmentation across algorithms; notable gains on OGBench; consistent improvements on D4RL.

