2) Video-CoM: Interactive Video Reasoning via Chain of Manipulations (cs.CV)
Authors: Hanoona Rasheed; Mohammed Zumri; Muhammad Maaz; Ming-Hsuan Yang; Fahad Shahbaz Khan; Salman Khan
- Problem: “Think about videos” paradigm treats video as static context—no rewatch/refocus/verification—limiting fine-grained spatio-temporal reasoning.
- Paradigm: “Think with videos”—Interactive Video Reasoning through a Chain of Manipulations (CoM), performing iterative visual actions to gather/refine evidence.
