- PET-guided switch to targeted therapy case (Proietti et al., 2020):
  - Patient: 78-year-old man with stage IV nodular melanoma; baseline 18F-FDG PET/CT showed cutaneous and skeletal metastases.
  - Initial treatment: Pembrolizumab (anti-PD-1).
  - Early assessment: At 3 months, PET/CT showed progressive metabolic disease (skeletal and cutaneous), confirmed by biopsy.
  - Molecular profile: Positive for BRAF V600K mutation.
  - Management change: Rapid switch to combined anti-BRAF/MEK targeted therapy.
  - Outcome: PET/CT 3 months after switch showed almost complete metabolic response; durable metabolic response continued at 10 months.
  - Takeaway: 18F-FDG PET/CT can enable early identification of immunotherapy non-responders and guide timely, personalized switches to targeted therapy in metastatic melanoma.

- Adjuvant systemic therapy guideline update (Ontario Health/CCO; Petrella et al., 2020):
  - Previous standard: High-dose interferon alfa-2b discussed/offered for resected cutaneous melanoma at high risk of recurrence.
  - Evidence evolution: Trials in resected and metastatic melanoma showed immune checkpoint inhibitors and targeted therapies provide greater benefit than interferon.
  - Implication: Guideline updated to favor checkpoint inhibitors and targeted therapies as adjuvant systemic options for high-risk melanoma.

- Unusual mediastinal metastatic melanoma case (Joyce et al., 2020):
  - Patient: 50-year-old man with prior cutaneous melanoma (resected in 2001).
  - Presentation: 12 weeks of exertional dyspnea, dull chest pain, non-productive cough.
  - Imaging: CT showed a large (10.7 × 7.6 cm), heterogeneously enhancing mass in the aortopulmonary window abutting the pericardium.
  - Biopsy: Open biopsy via left anterior thoracotomy of epicardial mass.
  - Immunohistochemistry: CD99 positive; focal CD56 positive; SOX10 positive; S100 positive; WT-1 positive.
  - Diagnosis: Metastatic melanoma involving the mediastinum (rare site, as both primary and metastatic lesions in mediastinum are uncommon).
  - Treatment: Initiated pembrolizumab; BRAF testing pending; assessment included V600E and V600K mutations in exon 15.
  - Significance: Highlights atypical recurrence site and the role of immunophenotyping and mutation testing in management.

