  - Anti-PD-1 monotherapy: Approximately 45% response rate in metastatic disease with low rates of severe toxicity.
  - Combination immunotherapy (anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4): Used in patients with adverse features; higher toxicity rates but adverse events are generally manageable with corticosteroids and treatment cessation; clinical benefit can persist after limited treatment duration.
  - Treatment selection should consider patient preference, symptom burden, and comorbidities (especially autoimmune disorders).

