2025-12-01 11:48:57,547 - agent.executor - INFO - Starting multi-server execution for task: ""I'm trying to understand the health risk factors for a 62-year-old male who's got quite a history with smoking and high blood pressure. He's currently on statins and has some lab results that are raising my concerns. His serum creatinine is at 1.5 mg/dL, and I noticed his total cholesterol is 240 mg/dL, with HDL around 40 mg/dL. His blood pressure is sitting at about 150 mmHg, and he's also dealing with elevated glucose levels around 180 mg/dL. 

I'm really curious about what this all means for his cardiovascular disease risk, especially with his kidney function being a bit off with that creatinine level. I've heard there's a way to estimate glomerular filtration rate that takes into account something called cystatin C, which he has at 0.8 mg/L. 

Could you help me break down what his eGFR might be and how that impacts his CVD risk? I want to make sure I’m looking at the numbers correctly because this all seems connected. Also, if there's any way to double-check the eGFR value, that would be great too. I just really need solid data to support any recommendations or discussions I have about his health moving forward.""
