--- Summary of Round 3 ---
Tool `NASA Data:get_coronal_mass_ejection` with Parameter {'start_date': '2025-11-01', 'end_date': '2025-12-01'} on NASA Data succeeded. Result (summarized from 1513 tokens): Summary of provided CME log (subset of 172 total CMEs)

Overall
- Total CMEs in dataset: 172 (only early entries from 2025-11-01 to 2025-11-03 shown; 162 more not listed).
- Instruments frequently referenced: SOHO LASCO C2/C3, STEREO A COR2, GOES CCOR-1, GOES SUVI (131/171/193/195/284/304).
- In the shown subset (10 events): speed range 253–785 km/s, average ≈562 km/s, median ≈580 km/s; Types: C (7), S (3).
- Notable themes: multiple NE-limb events with field-line opening; one likely far-sided jet; one likely Earth-facing disk CME; several minor outflows from a plage region near AR 14271; one CME pair with overtaking behavior; one C7.1 flare association (AR 14274).

Event-by-event (condensed)
- ID: 2025-11-01T03:12:00-CME-001
  - Start: 2025-11-01 03:12Z
  - Note: Narrow, jet-like CME to NE in SOHO LASCO C2/C3; not clearly seen in STEREO A COR2 or GOES CCOR-1; no EUV source; likely far-sided.
  - Analysis: 2025-11-01 07:51Z; Speed 785 km/s; Type C
  - Link: https://webtools.ccmc.gsfc.nasa.gov/DONKI/view/CME/42297/-1

- ID: 2025-11-01T18:00:00-CME-001
  - Start: 2025-11-01 18:00Z
  - Note: CME to East in SOHO/STA/GOES coronagraphs; source unclear in EUV but likely on Earth-facing disk; may be linked to activity near a coronal hole in NE (GOES SUVI imagery).
  - Analysis: 2025-11-01 23:28Z; Speed 624 km/s; Type C
  - Link: https://webtools.ccmc.gsfc.nasa.gov/DONKI/view/CME/42299/-1

- ID: 2025-11-02T12:23:00-CME-001
  - Start: 2025-11-02 12:23Z | Source: N25E90
  - Note: Large NE CME in STEREO A COR2, GOES CCOR-1, and in SOHO LASCO after a data gap; source is moving/opening field lines beyond NE limb starting ~08:00Z, accelerating near 10:00Z (SUVI 284/171/304); post-eruptive arcades with a C-class flare visible in SUVI 131 ~11:30Z.
  - Analysis: 2025-11-02 17:11Z; Speed 757 km/s; Type C
  - Link: https://webtools.ccmc.gsfc.nasa.gov/DONKI/view/CME/42308/-1

- ID: 2025-11-02T13:36:00-CME-001
  - Start: 2025-11-02 13:36Z
  - Note: Brightest follow-up front overlapping the 12:23Z CME to NE in all coronagraphs; no separate source apart from the earlier NE limb opening; coronal signatures include limb post-eruptive arcades after ~12:48Z.
  - Analysis: 2025-11-02 21:13Z; Speed 404 km/s; Type S
  - Link: https://webtools.ccmc.gsfc.nasa.gov/DONKI/view/CME/42315/-1

- ID: 2025-11-02T15:36:00-CME-001
  - Start: 2025-11-02 15:36Z | Source: S10E40
