Endpoint
- Method/Path: POST /app/installations/{installation_id}/access_tokens
- Tag: apps
- OperationId: apps/create-installation-access-token
- Docs: https://docs.github.com/rest/apps/apps#create-an-installation-access-token-for-an-app
- Purpose: Create an installation access token for a GitHub App installation (org or user).
- Auth: Requires authenticating as a GitHub App using a JWT.
- Token expiry: Installation tokens expire 1 hour after creation; expired tokens return 401 Unauthorized.
- Repository access:
  - By default, the token has access to all repositories the installation can access.
  - You can restrict access using repositories (names) or repository_ids (IDs) in the request body (max 500).
  - Token cannot be granted access to repos the installation doesn’t have.
- Permissions:
  - By default, token inherits all permissions granted to the app.
  - You can limit permissions via the permissions object in the request body.
  - Token cannot be granted permissions the app wasn’t granted.

Path parameter
- installation_id (integer, required): The unique identifier of the installation.

Request body (application/json; optional)
- repositories: array of repository names to grant access.
- repository_ids: array of repository IDs to grant access.
- permissions: object specifying desired permission levels. Unless stated otherwise, allowed values are read or write.
