Webhook: branch-protection-configuration-disabled
- Route: x-webhooks.branch-protection-configuration-disabled.post
- Summary: Event occurs when there is a change to branch protection configurations for a repository.
- Description: All branch protections were disabled for a repository.
- OperationId: branch-protection-configuration/disabled
- External docs for event: https://docs.github.com/webhooks/webhook-events-and-payloads#branch_protection_configuration
- Permissions: To subscribe, a GitHub App must have at least read-level access for the “Administration” repository permission.
- Headers (request parameters expected on delivery):
  - User-Agent
  - X-GitHub-Hook-Id
  - X-GitHub-Event
  - X-GitHub-Hook-Installation-Target-Id
  - X-GitHub-Hook-Installation-Target-Type
  - X-GitHub-Delivery
  - X-Hub-Signature-256
- Request body:
  - Content type: application/json
  - Schema: object (“branch protection configuration disabled event”)
  - Properties:
    - action: string, enum [disabled]
    - enterprise (Enterprise):
      - When present: webhook configured on an enterprise account or an org in an enterprise.
      - Properties: description (nullable), html_url (uri), website_url (nullable uri), id (integer), node_id (string), name (string), slug (string), created_at (date-time, nullable), updated_at (date-time, nullable), avatar_url (uri)
      - Required: id, node_id, name, slug, html_url, created_at, updated_at, avatar_url
    - installation (Simple Installation):
      - When present: event delivered to a GitHub App.
      - Properties: id (integer), node_id (string)
      - Required: id, node_id
    - organization (Organization Simple):
      - Properties: login (string), id (integer), node_id (string), url (uri), repos_url (uri), events_url (uri), hooks_url (string/uri), issues_url (string), members_url (templated string), public_members_url (templated string), avatar_url (string), description (string, nullable)
      - Required: login, url, id, node_id, repos_url, events_url, hooks_url, issues_url, members_url, public_members_url, avatar_url, description
    - repository (Repository):
      - Core identifiers: id (int64), node_id (string), name (string), full_name (string)
      - license (License Simple, nullable):
        - Properties: key (string), name (string), url (nullable uri), spdx_id (nullable string), node_id (string), html_url (uri)
